<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Entitlements for the main Shirox app target (Shirox_iOS).

		This file is a TEMPLATE — no Xcode target references it yet. The
		current pbxproj builds the iOS/macOS/tvOS/Catalyst targets without
		any `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS` build setting, and CI runs with
		`CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO` so entitlements are not enforced there.
		That keeps `buildipa.sh` working unchanged.

		When a developer is ready to wire up the Widget Extension (which
		needs a shared App Group so the app and extension can exchange
		UserDefaults data), they should:

		  1. Set `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS = Shirox/Shirox.entitlements` on the
		     Shirox_iOS target in Xcode (Build Settings → Signing →
		     Code Signing Entitlements).
		  2. Add the App Groups capability to the target in
		     Signing & Capabilities (Xcode will edit this file in step).
		  3. Make sure the App Group ID below matches
		     `ShiroxWidgetConfig.appGroup` and the entry in
		     `Shirox/Widgets/Widget.entitlements`.

		Only the iOS app target needs the App Group today — tvOS and macOS
		don't host widgets. macOS Catalyst could host widgets in 14+ but the
		current Catalyst build (`buildcatalyst.sh`) is unsigned, so adding
		entitlements there would break the DMG flow. Leave Catalyst alone
		unless you've thought through signing.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.shirox.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
